title: Agathe
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Agathe: Out of my kitchen! Oh. The map maker. Sit, then, if you must. #line:Agathe.1e21c573_0100_Agathe
Agathe: The Countess wants a feast tonight for the abbey's men, and I have no ale and no flour. The village has both. #line:Agathe.1e21c573_0200_Agathe
Agathe: Hedda's ale and Bram's flour. Bring me those, and you'll eat at the high table. #line:Agathe.1e21c573_0300_Agathe
-> I will go down to the village for you. #line:Agathe.1e21c573_0400
    Agathe: Quick, then. The road is an hour each way. #line:Agathe.1e21c573_0500_Agathe
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Active>>
-> I have work here. #line:Agathe.1e21c573_0600
    Agathe: Everybody has work here. Nobody has flour. #line:Agathe.1e21c573_0700_Agathe
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Offered>>
<<quest_changed feast>>
===

title: Agathe
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Offered
---
Agathe: Well? Ale and flour? #line:Agathe.36448d52_0100_Agathe
-> I will fetch them. #line:Agathe.36448d52_0200
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed feast>>
    Agathe: Quick, then. #line:Agathe.36448d52_0300_Agathe
-> Not yet. #line:Agathe.36448d52_0400
===

title: Agathe
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Active
---
<<if has_item("ale") and has_item("flour")>>
    Agathe: Ale! Flour! You beautiful creature. #line:Agathe.42d0f5a2_0100_Agathe
    <<take ale>>
    <<take flour>>
    <<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>>
        Agathe: And Hedda sent her mother's fair cake? She's never let that recipe out of the inn. You must have charmed her. #line:Agathe.42d0f5a2_0200_Agathe
    <<endif>>
    <<set $feast_served to true>>
    <<set $quest_feast to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed feast>>
<<else>>
    <<if has_item("ale")>>
        Agathe: Still no flour? The abbey's men will eat the tablecloth. #line:Agathe.42d0f5a2_0300_Agathe
    <<elseif has_item("flour")>>
        Agathe: Still no ale? The abbey's men will drink the well. #line:Agathe.42d0f5a2_0400_Agathe
    <<else>>
        Agathe: Nothing yet? Hedda's ale and Bram's flour. It isn't hard. #line:Agathe.42d0f5a2_0500_Agathe
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Agathe
act: All
location: Castle
scenario: The feast
when: $quest_feast != QuestState.NotStarted and $quest_feast != QuestState.Offered and $quest_feast != QuestState.Active
---
=> Agathe: Everything in this castle is cold except my kitchen. #line:Agathe.911485a8_0100_Agathe
=> Agathe: Corvin eats standing up. Never trust a man who eats standing up. #line:Agathe.911485a8_0200_Agathe
=> Agathe: The feast was a triumph. The abbot's men cried into the soup. <<if $feast_served>> #line:Agathe.911485a8_0300_Agathe
===

title: Events
act: Castle
location: Village
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: once
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: here() == "Village" and been_to("Castle")
---
// The village after a day away: what changed while the cartographer was at the castle. Not before the castle: the
// summons sets the act in the village, and the journey waits for the end of the dialogue and of its events.
The village looks smaller after the castle. #line:Events.1676df30_0100
Pell's cart is gone from the green. He went up the hill to sell to the castle. #line:Events.1676df30_0200
<<if $culprit == Culprit.Lio>>
    The boundary stones stand where the sergeant left them. Nobody moved them last night. #line:Events.1676df30_0300
<<else>>
    The boundary stones have moved again. One more pace up the bank. #line:Events.1676df30_0400
<<endif>>
===

title: Hedda
act: Castle
location: Inn
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Active and not has_item("ale")
---
Hedda: Ale for the castle? Agathe sent you? She'd send the river if it could carry a cask. #line:Hedda.cb91d0c3_0100_Hedda
<<give ale>>
<<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Hedda: And take this cake for the high table. My mother's recipe. Tell Agathe whose it is. #line:Hedda.cb91d0c3_0200_Hedda
<<endif>>
===

title: Hedda
act: All
location: Inn
scenario: The feast
when: always
---
=> Hedda: Soup's on. It's always on. #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0100_Hedda
=> Hedda: The regulars are Wim and Saul. They have argued about the same cow for nine years. <<if $act == Act.Survey>> #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0200_Hedda
=> Hedda: Corvin drinks here when the castle is too quiet for him. He pays, I'll give him that. <<if $act == Act.Survey>> #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0300_Hedda
=> Hedda: Lio was out late again. I saw the lantern go down to the river. <<if $act == Act.Survey and not $saw_lio>> #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0400_Hedda
=> Hedda: Bram will lose the mill if the road goes straight. He won't say it, but he's afraid. <<if $act == Act.Survey>> #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0500_Hedda
=> Hedda: The castle has you running errands? That's a castle for you. <<if $act == Act.Castle>> #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0600_Hedda
=> Hedda: The cake is in the oven for the fair. <<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>> #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0700_Hedda
=> Hedda: The regulars talk of nothing but Jory. <<if $act == Act.Fair>> #line:Hedda.9a83e94e_0800_Hedda
===

title: Bram
act: Castle
location: Village
scenario: The feast
quest: feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
when: $quest_feast == QuestState.Active and not has_item("flour")
---
<<if $wheel_mended>>
    Bram: Flour for the castle's feast? The wheel ground all night. Take a sack, and tell the Countess it's Oster flour. #line:Bram.b6d66cd3_0100_Bram
    <<give flour>>
<<else>>
    Bram: Flour? With the wheel stuck? I have none to give, not even to a Countess. #mood:sad #line:Bram.b6d66cd3_0200_Bram
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitFounder
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitFounder") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
    The founder of the house of Varne, in gold armour, with a map unrolled at his feet. The border on it runs under a hill. #line:PortraitFounder_0100
<<else>>
    The founder again. He looks at you as if you owe him rent. #line:PortraitFounder_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitTwins
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitTwins") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
    Two sisters, the same face twice. One of them married an abbot's brother, and the border moved a mile. #line:PortraitTwins_0100
<<else>>
    The twins. One of them is smiling. You are not sure it was the same one last time. #line:PortraitTwins_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitSaint
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitSaint") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
<<endif>>
// The castle's runner chooses among line groups with its own saliency strategy: the lines come round in order
=> A pale lady in blue, holding a lantern. The plate says "Saint of the Deep Ways". #line:PortraitSaint_0100
=> The lantern in the painting is green, like no flame you have ever seen. #line:PortraitSaint_0200
=> The lady in blue again. Her lantern lights a carved wall behind her. #line:PortraitSaint_0300
===

title: PortraitHound
act: Castle
location: Castle
scenario: The portraits
quest: portraits
---
<<if visited_count("PortraitHound") == 0>>
    <<set $portraits_seen to $portraits_seen + 1>>
    <<detour PortraitSeen>>
    A hound. Just a hound. The plate says "Biscuit, who found the well". #line:PortraitHound_0100
<<elseif visited_count("PortraitHound") == 1>>
    Biscuit again. A good dog. A great dog, by the look of the frame. #line:PortraitHound_0200
<<else>>
    You have looked at this dog [plural value={visited_count("PortraitHound") + 1} one="% time" other="% times" /] now. #line:PortraitHound_0300
<<endif>>
===

title: PortraitSeen
act: Castle
location: Castle
quest: portraits
---
// Said the first time each portrait is looked at, after it is counted.
<<if $portraits_seen >= 4>>
    <<set $quest_portraits to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed portraits>>
<<elseif $quest_portraits == QuestState.NotStarted>>
    <<set $quest_portraits to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed portraits>>
<<endif>>
===
